  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Alice and Bob are playing a game that involves an array AAA of length NNN containing non-negative integers. The following sequence of events occurs **exactly once**:\n\n\nAlice chooses two (not necessarily distinct) indices iii and jjj. Then, Alice sets Ai:=Ai⊕AjA_i := A_i \\oplus A_jAi​:=Ai​⊕Aj​ where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\nThen, Bob chooses two (not necessarily distinct) indices iii and jjj and sets Ai:=Ai⊕AjA_i := A_i \\oplus A_jAi​:=Ai​⊕Aj​.\nThe score of the board is calculated as A1⊕A2⊕⋯⊕AnA_1 \\oplus A_2 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus A_nA1​⊕A2​⊕⋯⊕An​.\nAlice wants to maximize the score while Bob wants to minimize the score. Assuming both players use optimal strategies, determine the final score.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the optimal score.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\le A_i \\lt 2^{30}0≤Ai​&lt;230",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n2\n1 1\n2\n1 2\n4\n1 0 3 4\n4\n16 17 18 19\n9\n15 27 18 23 99 64 16 0 37",
        "output": "0\n2\n3\n1\n36",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : Alice can choose i=1,j=1i = 1, j = 1i=1,j=1 and change A1=A1⊕A2=0A_1 = A_1 \\oplus A_2 = 0A1​=A1​⊕A2​=0. Hence, AAA becomes [0,1][0, 1][0,1]. Now, Bob can choose i=2,j=2i = 2, j = 2i=2,j=2 and change AAA to [0,0][0, 0][0,0]. This has a score of 000.\nTest Case 2 : Alice can choose i=1,j=2i = 1, j = 2i=1,j=2 and change A=[3,2]A = [3, 2]A=[3,2]. Now, Bob chooses i=2,j=1i = 2, j = 1i=2,j=1 and changes A=[3,1]A = [3, 1]A=[3,1] which has a score of 222."
      }
    ]
  },
